WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:06.560
I'm here in one of the weirdest pieces
of land I've ever been flying my drone

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.720
over the Indian Ocean.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:14.020
There's a battle
going on out here.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.440
It's not a battle for

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:22.960
land or for people. This is a battle
about fish.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:28.340
One fishermen was killed and five others injured after Sri Lankan
Navy opened fire near an island off the

00:00:28.349 --> 00:00:29.440
Tamil Nadu coast.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:32.610
On one side you have
Sri Lankan fishermen in these coastal

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:39.210
villages, where fishing is the economic
lifeblood. And on the other side you have

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:43.500
their counterparts Indian fishermen in
these villages along the southeastern

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:44.660
coast of India.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.420
On a clear day you can see across this

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:54.070
strait, it's only 20 kilometers or so.
And out here on the water there's an

00:00:54.070 --> 00:01:00.200
invisible line that marks where India's
territorial waters end and where Sri Lanka's begin.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:07.979
Underneath this border
there's treasure — not gold, but seafood.

00:01:07.979 --> 00:01:12.250
The communities on either side of this
strait used to be friends, but now

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:18.009
they're locked in conflict. One side has
bigger, faster boats. The other side has a

00:01:18.009 --> 00:01:23.640
well-armed Navy equipped with war boats
that they're using to patrol this border.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:41.280
This is the fish war between India and Sri Lanka.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:04.820
This is Rama's bridge.

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:09.320
You look across, you
can see Sri Lanka.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:13.300
One legend goes that

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:18.080
the Hindu god Rama hired an army of
monkey men to build a bridge from India

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:23.560
to Sri Lanka, so that he could go in and
rescue his wife from a demon king.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:28.069
Geology suggests that there indeed may
have been a walkable land bridge here,

00:02:28.069 --> 00:02:32.750
until a few thousand years ago when it
was eroded back into the sea, erasing any

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:38.000
land border between modern-day India and
Sri Lanka. The only border that exists

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:43.459
now between India and Sri Lanka is in
the water. It was decided on in the '70s

00:02:43.459 --> 00:02:46.180
and it looks like this.

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:48.799
This border made
it officially illegal for fishermen from

00:02:48.799 --> 00:02:52.790
either side to cross over into each
other's waters to fish and it was the

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:56.740
start of what would eventually turn into
a violent conflict.

00:02:56.740 --> 00:02:57.829
"The injured fishermen

00:02:57.829 --> 00:02:59.820
have been admitted to a hospital in
Rameswaram."

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:04.900
In the 1960s India, was

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:08.959
facing a financial crisis and in
response, the government was looking for

00:03:08.959 --> 00:03:13.489
new ways to stimulate the economy. So
they turned to seafood exports like

00:03:13.489 --> 00:03:17.569
prawns. The Indian government gave
subsidies to fishermen to buy new boats

00:03:17.569 --> 00:03:21.530
so that they could harvest a huge number
of prawns, which would feed demand all

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:26.720
over the world. So Indian fishermen in
this town of Rameswaram cashed in on

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:30.769
the opportunity, dramatically ramping up
their fishing activities with these new

00:03:30.769 --> 00:03:35.180
boat is called trawlers which are able
to drop nets with heavy weights on them

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:40.190
to rake the bottom of the seabed in
search for prawns and other seafood. It's

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:44.660
an incredibly effective method for
harvesting fish and shrimp, but these

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:49.280
heavy metal weights rip up the seabed,
damaging the sea floor's ecosystem and

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:54.019
this method if uncontrolled depletes
fish supplies very quickly. The Indian

00:03:54.019 --> 00:03:58.010
fishermen quickly adopted these new
boats and soon there were thousands of

00:03:58.010 --> 00:03:59.240
these trawlers.

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:10.579
Armed with their new boats and tied to
international demand, the Indian

00:04:10.579 --> 00:04:14.390
fishermen aggressively fished these
waters, tearing up the seafloor and

00:04:14.390 --> 00:04:19.549
depleting much of their fisheries. By the
late 1970s, the Indian fishermen needed

00:04:19.549 --> 00:04:23.960
new waters to fish. This water border had
recently been agreed upon by the two

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:27.680
countries, but even still the Indian
fishermen began moving across it

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:31.910
illegally fishing in Sri Lankan waters.
The massive amount of fishing

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:36.949
contributed to an explosion in seafood
exports from India. While India was

00:04:36.949 --> 00:04:41.690
cashing in on seafood products from Sri
Lankan waters, Sri Lanka was descending

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:42.820
into war.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:50.300
By the early 1980s, armed rebels
were taking over large swaths of land in

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:54.199
the north of the country, trying to
create a new country for the oppressed

00:04:54.199 --> 00:04:58.130
Tamil people, the ethnic minority group
that the residents of these fishing

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.940
villages identify with.

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:02.660
"And every day
they take an oath pledging to sacrifice

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:07.580
their mind body and soul for Tamil Eelam,
a separate state for a separate people."

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:12.440
It descended into a violent, long-lasting
civil war that would result in over

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:16.699
150,000 deaths and
these fishing villages in Sri Lanka were

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:18.080
caught right in the middle of it.

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:31.760
As a security precaution during the war
the Sri Lankan Navy started setting up

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:36.090
security zones in much of the water,
banning most fishing activities and

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:37.600
prohibiting boats with motors.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:39.960
"Beaches once crammed with foreign

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:42.800
tourists are now patrolled by the
watchful military."

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:44.520
All of this was done

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:49.380
in an attempt to weaken the Tamil rebels,
but the result was a severe gutting of

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:54.030
the economies here, which are totally
reliant on fish. The catch in these

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:58.950
districts declined immensely during the
war and not only did this affect the

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:03.870
economies, but this fishing ban left Sri
Lankan waters open for Indian trawlers

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:05.720
to fish freely.

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:17.220
The violent civil war
and the fishing ban in Sri Lanka dragged

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:21.660
on through the '90s and into the early
2000's, allowing the Indian fishermen to

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:27.580
illegally fish these waters with little
repercussion. But then everything changed.

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:34.440
"Tamil Tiger fighters retreat from their
last stand. For now the fighting seems to

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:39.810
be over."
The war ended and the security zones in

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:43.950
the water were lifted. Sri Lankans could
fish freely again, breathing new life

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:49.470
into an economy that runs on fish. But as
these fishermen went out on their boats

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:54.300
what they found were fleets of Indian
trawlers in their waters, tearing up the

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:59.070
sea floor, illegally digging for seafood
treasure. And these Sri Lankan fishermen

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:04.920
coming out of a fishing ban and a 25 year
civil war, had much smaller weaker boats.

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:08.040
They could never compete.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:26.320
This is where things really start to heat up.

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:34.440
Sri Lankan Navy, which had previously been
fighting a war, now turned its efforts

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:38.370
towards cracking down on Indian
fishermen that were poaching in Sri

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:43.300
Lankan waters. The fish wars had begun.

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:44.610
"Naval Command arrested four Indian

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:47.320
fishing poachers in Sri Lanka territorial waters."

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:58.920
"There are mass protests against the killing of this fisherman."

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:01.260
The Sri Lankan Navy came down hard, routinely

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:05.850
arresting Indian fishermen and detaining
them, sometimes for years. Many of the

00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:09.510
fishermen that I talked to while I was
in India routinely go poaching across

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:12.440
the border and many of them said that
they had been caught by the Navy.

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:25.060
When the Navy detains the fishermen, they
also take their boats. They eventually

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:29.360
released the fishermen, but the boats
remain impounded in navy bases around

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:30.420
the country.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:48.520
Across the strait, this
poaching by Indian fishermen has had

00:08:48.530 --> 00:08:51.160
deep ramifications in these villages.

00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:03.740
Experts estimate that the direct
monetary loss to Sri Lankan fishermen

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:08.780
due to Indian poaching is anywhere from
16 to 56 million US dollars per year.

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:41.690
This conflict over seafood has turned two
Tamil communities, once allies, into

00:09:41.690 --> 00:09:43.240
enemies.

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:15.899
The Indian government has done little to
resolve this conflict. They occasionally

00:10:15.899 --> 00:10:20.250
step in to free a group of detained
fishermen, but none of their actions have

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:23.220
led to a concrete solution to the
conflict.

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:39.600
The Indian government, both national and
local, seems to be turning a blind eye to

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:42.080
these fishermen's practice of crossing
the border.

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:43.110
That's because these

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:47.130
communities are already neglected and
underserved by their faraway government.

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:51.810
Stopping a practice that has bolstered
their economy for years would create

00:10:51.810 --> 00:10:54.760
more disdain and frustration among the
people.

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:08.399
So not much is likely to change anytime
soon and as the Navy and the fishermen

00:11:08.399 --> 00:11:13.199
continue to spar in these waters, the
real losers in this situation continue

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:15.600
to be these communities over here.

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:44.800
The people here were barred from fishing during the
decades-long civil war and now they have

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:48.550
no chance of competing with their Indian
neighbors, who have spent decades

00:11:48.550 --> 00:11:52.320
destroying their sea beds and stealing
their fish.

00:11:55.760 --> 00:11:59.560
This was one of the most interesting places I had ever been,

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:02.760
going to Sri Lanka and the southern coast of India.

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:09.180
Got to see these really interesting places, but also seeing how important fish are to these economies.

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:14.980
But India and Sri Lanka aren't the only places that are affected by the increasing demand for fish.

00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:18.600
There are a lot of different places around the world who are dealing with similar issues.

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:22.040
And if you want to learn more about this issue and how it plays out in other countries,

